{"ts": "2026-11-04T22:43:53.454920Z", "run_id": "r-20261104T2240Z-52a0", "unit": "openspec:add-interpreter-core", "seq": 8, "type": "delegate.result", "question": "Q-001", "id": "Q-001", "status": "answered", "reason": "I read the head code and traced every held test through it. block.ts lines 112-151 implement the full effect path of design Decision 7 (before in step node, unknown throws EFFECT_UNKNOWN, reuse skips invoke, invoke with idemKey, after in step node#done then output check, rejections mapped to TOOL_FAILED with a fixed message). ops.ts pushes the step name before calling the callback, errors.ts sets code and node, index.ts exports NO_EFFECT_GATE, memoryWorkflowOps and nodeRuntimeFor, and the catalogue's erp.create_payment@1 has effect pay with an output schema that refuses { payment_id: \"p\" }. So the nine tests pass on head and the pre-satisfied claim is true; the inconclusive base run is explained by scaffold stubs that throw. The replay applies the patch under every gate, so a wrong accept is caught. I could not run anything, and I flag that the step-tagging test is weaker than the scenario.", "called": true, "tasks": ["2.3"], "target": null, "kind": "harness", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code", "cost_usd": 1.9971035, "decision": "accept", "answer_sha256": "7830990fc260285dc8f3459a63ff40dba536433a153aca5261f9c77e4bb594a2", "checked": [{"ref": "src/interpreter/runtimes/block.ts:112", "quote": "await services.ops.runStep<JsonValue>(nodeId, async () => {", "claim": "The effect path's first step, named after the node, already exists at the unit head."}, {"ref": "src/interpreter/runtimes/block.ts:120", "quote": "if (decision.action === \"unknown\") {", "claim": "An unknown decision is refused with INTERPRETER_EFFECT_UNKNOWN before any invoke."}, {"ref": "src/interpreter/runtimes/block.ts:141", "quote": "await services.ops.runStep(`${nodeId}#done`, async () => {", "claim": "The gate's after runs in the step node#done, followed by the output check."}, {"ref": "src/interpreter/runtimes/block.ts:31", "quote": "\"INTERPRETER_TOOL_FAILED\", \"node execution failed\"", "claim": "Gate and invoker rejections map to TOOL_FAILED with a fixed message that carries no secret."}, {"ref": "src/interpreter/ops.ts:29", "quote": "executed.push(name);", "claim": "memoryWorkflowOps records the step name before running the callback, so a failing step still appears in executed."}, {"ref": "src/interpreter/errors.ts:31", "quote": "this.node = node ?? null;", "claim": "InterpreterError carries the node the tests assert on."}, {"ref": "src/interpreter/index.ts:33", "quote": "export { NO_EFFECT_GATE } from \"./gate.ts\";", "claim": "The symbols the new tests import are exported from the module index."}, {"ref": "test/support/catalogue/blocks.v0.json:74", "quote": "\"effect\": \"pay\",", "claim": "erp.create_payment@1 is not a read block, so it takes the effect path."}, {"ref": "test/support/catalogue/blocks.v0.json:77", "quote": "\"required\": [\"payment_id\", \"status\"]", "claim": "The output { payment_id: \"p\" } fails the block's output schema, as the invalid-output test expects."}, {"ref": "openspec/changes/add-interpreter-core/specs/interpreter/spec.md:36", "quote": "call `EffectGate.after` in the step `<node>#done`", "claim": "The requirement the head code implements and the tests exercise."}, {"ref": "openspec/changes/add-interpreter-core/design.md:18", "quote": "`after(call, { ...ctx, idemKey }, { output })` always (also after `reuse`", "claim": "The design requires after even on reuse, which block.ts and the reuse test follow."}, {"ref": "openspec/changes/add-interpreter-core/tasks.md:11", "quote": "- [x] 2.2 Write `src/interpreter/runtimes/block.test.ts`", "claim": "Task 2.2, already done, owns block.ts, which explains why the effect path predates task 2.3."}]}
